iMac 18,3 CS8409/CS42L83: internal mic is silent while a 3.5mm headset is plugged in.

Applies to the snd_hda_macbookpro DKMS driver (davidjo/snd_hda_macbookpro),
against the tree at commit be90113. Confirmed on hardware.

Internal mic records fine with nothing in the jack, and goes completely
silent the moment a headset is plugged in -- peak amplitude drops to exactly
0.00000 while the capture stream itself runs happily and reports no error.

cs_8409_pcm_capture_pre_prepare_hook branched on spec->jack_present and then
on spec->have_mike. With a mic-equipped headset detected it ran the headset
capture path (cs_8409_headcapture_setup, headset mic -> CS8409 ADC 0x1a) and
never called cs_8409_capture_setup, which is the only thing that brings the
internal mic up; with a headset that presents no mic it fell through a
"I think this is impossible" comment and set nothing up at all. Either way
the PCM stream stays bound to intmike_adc_nid 0x23, so the driver configures
one microphone and then records from a different one. The reason the stream
is silent rather than wrong is visible in the hardware: during a failing
capture with a headset in, vendor coef 0x82 reads back 0x0000 (DMIC2_SCL_EN
never set -- only cs_8409_intmike_stream_on_nid sets it) and pin node 0x45
shows Pin-ctls: 0x00, because that same function is what writes
SET_PIN_WIDGET_CONTROL 0x20 to it. The internal mic is simply never
switched on.

Drop the have_mike branch so cs_8409_capture_setup(codec) runs
unconditionally, and make the teardown symmetric by always calling
cs_8409_capture_cleanup. The jack_present test survives only to keep
block_unsol set. Removing the paired headplay/headcapture setup+cleanup
from the capture hooks is deliberate: the playback hooks already do that
work when something actually plays, so capture no longer drags the
headphone amp up as a side effect.

The rest is what makes it survive a plug event. cs_8409_intmike_linein_disable()
and switch_input_src() come out of cs_8409_boot_setup_real,
cs_8409_plugin_event_continued and cs_8409_unplug_handle_disconnect -- they
tore the internal mic back down (and re-pointed ALSA's input source) on every
plug/unplug, which would undo the setup above -- and each remaining
cs_8409_inputs_power_nids_off() is guarded with !spec->capturing so a plug
event during a live recording cannot power the input nids off underneath it.
This also retires the "PLUGIN WHILE CAPTURING UNIMPLEMENTED!!" case.

Upstream: ExternPointer, davidjo/snd_hda_macbookpro issue #29, posted
2026-09-05, tested by its author on a MacBookPro14,3 on kernel 7.1.9.
The upstream diff was cut against a tree whose
cs_8409_pcm_capture_pre_prepare_hook still had an inner
"else cs_8409_capture_setup(codec);" arm that be90113 has already replaced
with the "I think this is impossible" comment, so its first hunk was
reapplied by hand here; the resulting file is byte-identical to the
author's (blob c2a33a8). The other five hunks applied unmodified.

Verified on iMac18,3, kernel 7.1.9-arch1-2, codec subsystem id 0x106b1000:
internal mic with a mic-equipped headset plugged in records at peak 0.904
(was 0.00000), matching the 0.905 it gives with nothing plugged in;
mid-capture pin 0x45 now reads Pin-ctls: 0x20: IN with its amps unmuted.
Speakers, the hardware analog sink and repeated back-to-back captures are
unaffected.

